! Floating-point diagnostic jb_af1c, routine F205B "TESTS OF SIGN AND
! MODIFIER VARIATIONS" for ADD TO MAGNITUDE (docs/jb_af1c_floating-
! point.pdf pp.67-72, octal 013153.00-013433.00): thirty-two sub-tests
! of +MG / +MGA / -MG / -MGA over every memory-sign (MS) / accumulator-
! sign (ACS) combination -- the accumulator sign set by L(U) or LN(U),
! the memory sign by the constant (FPK4/FPK19 positive, FPK23/FPK24
! negative) -- each checking the accumulator's left half bits 0-59 at
! offset 68 against the expected constant (CT0110 + BRGZ,SERS) and the
! accumulator sign bit, bit 4 of the sign byte register ($SB+.4), by
! BB/BZB. The sub-test comments are the listing's own.
!
! What the block establishes (Ref. Manual p.88, ADD TO MAGNITUDE): the
! operand is added to the MAGNITUDE of the accumulator (the accumulator
! sign is treated as positive), the N and A modifiers act on the
! storage operand (A: absolute, N: negate, A first), a negative sum is
! a FORCED ZERO with the accumulator's exponent and sign (FPK29:
! exponent 1, zero fraction, e.g. B6: +1/3 in the acc minus 2/3), and
! the result always carries the accumulator's ORIGINAL sign, since
! only its magnitude took part: BZB (bit 0) for the L-loaded sub-tests
! B1-B8 and B17-B24, BB (bit 1) for every LN-loaded one, forced zeros
! included (B14, B16, B26, B32).
!
! Substitutions (SSIP framework, real listed addresses): SERS (octal
! 1304) -> FAIL halt, SEN (octal 1310) -> scratch, PASS -> the
! routine's exit at 013433.00 (the listing's "BD,$+1.0"). Constants
! from the pool p.176. The entry FAMG2's "BD,$+.32" is kept verbatim;
! the other sub-tests begin with the listing's "B,$+.32" separator
! (except B8, which the listing runs straight into).
!
! Instructions: BD, B, L(U)/LN(U), +MG/+MGA/-MG/-MGA, NOP (B21), CT0110
! with offset 68, SIC, BRGZ, BB/BZB on the sign byte bit.
! verify_fp_arith_f205b_listing.py checks every word bit-for-bit.
!
! Observed: with the model as it stood after F205A, the first run
! halted at B20's arithmetic check -- and the cause was the FPK23
! transcription, see the note above (the model's exact sum of the
! "230" reading was one unit short of FPK22). One model change was
! made ahead of the run from the listing alone: the + arm now keeps
! the accumulator's own sign through +MG (every LN-loaded sub-test
! expects sign bit 1, forced zeros included), where it previously
! wrote the adder's sign. With FPK23 corrected all thirty-two
! sub-tests pass and the run halts at PASS with SEN still 0.

! Transcription note on FPK23 (pool p.176, octal 22034): the scan's last
! group reads as "230" or "250" -- 3 and 5 are near-identical in this
! typewriter font. It is "250": a -2/3 whose fraction keeps the
! 525252... alternation ends in 101 + sign 1 (compare FK43, the same
! value at 22215, printed "...250"), and the block's own arithmetic
! requires it -- B20/B22 add FPK4 to the magnitude of FPK23 and expect
! the all-ones FPK22, which only "250" gives (the model, doing exact
! arithmetic on the "230" reading, came out one unit short and
! halted at B20's check: the diagnostic disambiguating its own scan).
!
! -- SSIP framework substitutes --
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0

! -- constants (pool p.176) --

        SLC, (8)22011.0
FPK4    DD(BU,64,8), (8)0000452525252525252520
        SLC, (8)22030.0
FPK19   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0000525252525252525240
        SLC, (8)22033.0
FPK22   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0000577777777777777760
        SLC, (8)22034.0
FPK23   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0000525252525252525250
        SLC, (8)22035.0
FPK24   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0000452525252525252530
        SLC, (8)22042.0
FPK29   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0000400000000000000000

! -- code (verbatim, at the listing's addresses) --
        SLC, (8)13153.0
FAMG2   BD, $+.32   ! FAMG2 / F205B1: MS+ACS+N+A+0
        L(U), FPK19
        +MG(U), FPK4
        CT0110(BU,60), FPK22, 68   ! check no. in acc
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        BZB, $SB+.4, $+2.   ! is sign bit equal 0
        SIC, SEN
        B, SERS
        B, $+.32   ! F205B2: MS+ACS+N+A+0
        L(U), FPK4
        +MG(U), FPK19
        CT0110(BU,60), FPK22, 68   ! check no. in acc
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
